{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not require an applicant to disclose or be asked about a criminal record before making a conditional offer, and afterward may consider only certain recent or serious convictions after an individualized assessment, with written notice and an appeal right.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes; does not include a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; a provider may consider methamphetamine-manufacture convictions on federally assisted housing and lifetime sex-offender registrants.","penalty":"Director may impose civil penalties up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior in five years), or $10,000 (two or more priors in seven years).","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.92,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history review and the applicant's right to submit evidence of inaccuracies or rehabilitation; the director may require the fee be returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes; does not include a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require the applicant's rental application fee be returned; civil penalties up to $1,000 to $10,000 apply.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.88,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful provider appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and a court overturns the director's order, that determination is grounds to evict a former applicant placed in the unit by the order, with at least 45 days' notice before eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant who resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order after the provider's successful appeal.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Former applicant residing in the unit because of the director's order, after the housing provider's successful appeal.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

